course: dictionary
lesson: 11797
title: Bequeath: passing things on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To bequeath something means to leave it to someone in your will, so they get it after you die. A will is the paper that says who gets your things. «Grandma bequeathed her old piano to me in her will.» The word will is a clue here: it tells you the piano was given in a document that says who gets what.
explain: Bequeath is a formal word. Your everyday word for the same idea is leave. «Grandma left me her piano» and «Grandma bequeathed me her piano» mean nearly the same thing, but bequeath sounds more serious and is used in stories, law and official writing.
explain: The word can also mean passing something on to people who come later, such as an idea or a tradition. «She bequeathed a love of stories to her grandchildren.» Nobody wrote this in a will. It means she gave them her love of stories, and they will keep it going.
fact: Bequeath means to leave money or belongings to someone in your will.
fact: Bequeath can also mean to pass ideas or traditions on to people who come later.
fact: The past tense is «bequeathed»: «He bequeathed his house to the village.»
fact: Bequeath is a formal word. Leave is the everyday word with a similar meaning.
fact: Look for clues like «will» or «after she died» to help you work out bequeath.
exercise: «Grandma bequeathed her old piano to me in her will.» What does bequeathed mean? | Bought a new piano for the shop | *Left something to someone in her will | Lost the piano during a move | Played the piano very loudly
exercise: «She bequeathed a love of stories to her grandchildren.» What did she pass on to them? | *A love of stories | A new school bag | Her old car | A house by the sea
exercise: Which word is the past tense of bequeath in «He ___ his house to the village»? | *bequeathed | bequeathing | bequeath | bequeaths
test: «Their grandfather bequeathed the farm to his daughter.» Who got the farm? | *His daughter | The neighbours | The bank | Nobody, it was sold
test: Which sentence uses bequeath to mean passing an idea on to later people? | «The old poet bequeathed a sack of potatoes to the shop.» | «The old poet bequeathed a loud shout at the market.» | *«The old poet bequeathed his ideas to the young writers.» | «The old poet bequeathed a new coat for the winter.»
exam: «The queen bequeathed her jewels to her granddaughter after she died.» What does bequeathed show? | Something was broken by accident | Something was lost on a trip | *Something was given to someone in a will after death | Something was sold at a market
